@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+# Private post-cutover retirement patch
+
+Apply only after independent production AWS data/API and browser acceptance and review by the release owner. Verification uses a disposable loopback PostgreSQL cluster and a separate local, protocol-compatible S3 server with sandbox-only credentials. No AWS, provider, GitHub or production database writes.
+
+Before implementation, exercise the worker's public staging workflows: read a gzip chunk under its original S3 key, verify catalog byte count and SHA-256, recover a pinned mutable manifest from its historical content-addressed key, fail on corruption and traversal, resolve standalone ordinal/documentId and archived lineup references, upsert a projection and cursor in the staging schema, and read them back directly in SQL. Start the four original supplemental/UEFA/coach entry points with only explicit AWS ingest configuration and deny outbound provider traffic. For UEFA use deterministic HTTP responses through a fixture transport; validate source season and mapped team ID from SQL. Prove a runtime-only/legacy-only config cannot start the writer and an unsupported object endpoint is refused. Record inputs, exact rerun, statuses, object keys and receipts. Treat local object service semantics as separate from live IAM/availability.
+
+No previously applied migrations, origins of provider requests, archive key names, collection schedules, or stored data keys may be changed. Retain official distinctions between staging writers and the SELECT-only application.
+
+Collector default acceptance (registered before setting typed queue ordering): invoke the real standalone Python collector without --skip-materialize on a seeded local staging database. Explicit --priority-league must publish only that league and preserve unrelated dirty rows. Daily/pulse must prefer one most recently dirtied partition for each historic target (MLS and Saudi) before a general budget of 20. Historical runs bounded to a league must use oldest dirty work first. A global historical invocation may publish at most 20; priority slots are additional only when those target rows exist. Collection request count, provider candidate selection and staged status fields remain unchanged. Explicit --skip-materialize remains staging-only for workflows that run publication in their next step. Package aliases must invoke the same standalone default. Source discovery may identify/queue unrelated staged changes, but a scoped publication must not rematerialize unrelated partitions or drain global catalogs.
